Let the MPEG-TS muxer carry the MPEG-4 Part 2 headers in the stream.

MPEG-4 Part 2 video begins with a Visual Object Sequence, a Visual Object and a Video Object Layer
header, which give the picture size and how the pictures are coded. An encoder writing for MP4 or
Matroska puts them in the extradata alone, because those containers carry it beside the stream.
MPEG-TS has no such place, and the muxer copied the packets as they came, so a stream copy of such
a track into MPEG-TS held no header at all, and FFmpeg's own decoder could not decode a single
picture of it. The muxer already fixes the same gap for H.264, HEVC and VVC through its
check_bitstream callback.

The callback now adds the dump_extra filter to an MPEG-4 Part 2 stream that has extradata. With
its default frequency the filter puts the extradata in front of each keyframe and leaves alone a
keyframe that already begins with it, so a stream whose headers are in band, such as one read
from MPEG-TS, comes through unchanged. The muxer now selects the filter, so a build that enables
only the muxer still has it.

Applied by BuildFFmpegTask before configure, after 0006, and independent of the patches before
it. Fixes yuroyami/KiteFFmpeg#159.

diff --git a/configure b/configure
index 374bd5c..ff2890d 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -3970,7 +3970,7 @@ mp3_demuxer_select="mpegaudio_parser"
 mp3_muxer_select="mpegaudioheader"
 mp4_muxer_select="mov_muxer"
 mpegts_demuxer_select="iso_media"
-mpegts_muxer_select="ac3_parser adts_muxer latm_muxer h264_mp4toannexb_bsf hevc_mp4toannexb_bsf vvc_mp4toannexb_bsf"
+mpegts_muxer_select="ac3_parser adts_muxer latm_muxer dump_extradata_bsf h264_mp4toannexb_bsf hevc_mp4toannexb_bsf vvc_mp4toannexb_bsf"
 mpegtsraw_demuxer_select="mpegts_demuxer"
 mxf_muxer_select="iso_writer pcm_rechunk_bsf rangecoder"
 mxf_muxer_suggest="eia608_to_smpte436m_bsf"
diff --git a/libavformat/mpegtsenc.c b/libavformat/mpegtsenc.c
index 1abaaf9..f1825f9 100644
--- a/libavformat/mpegtsenc.c
+++ b/libavformat/mpegtsenc.c
@@ -2374,6 +2374,12 @@ static int mpegts_check_bitstream(AVFormatContext *s, AVStream *st,
                         ((st->codecpar->extradata[0] & e->mask) == e->value))))
             return ff_stream_add_bitstream_filter(st, e->bsf_name, NULL);
     }
+    /* MPEG-4 Part 2 keeps its VOS, VO and VOL headers in the extradata of an MP4 or Matroska
+     * track, and MPEG-TS has nowhere to carry them but in the stream, so a copy without them
+     * cannot be decoded. dump_extra puts them in front of each keyframe and leaves alone a
+     * packet that already begins with them. */
+    if (st->codecpar->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_MPEG4 && st->codecpar->extradata_size > 0)
+        return ff_stream_add_bitstream_filter(st, "dump_extra", NULL);
     return 1;
 }
 
